  "provenance": "OC-021: synthetic D-shape case exercising coupled-search schema v12 -- the optional mechanical.max_transverse_pressure_pa declared bound, end to end. Same centerline as OC-019 (inner leg 0.7 m, R=0.08 m corners, R=0.43 m outer bulge; robinson-superpower-ap-v3 measured dataset) at a 1.0 T bore target so pack fields sit inside dataset coverage (4-8 T at the tape) and transverse pressures land in the 24-58 MPa range -- the scale where REBCO broad-face delamination is a real concern. The declared 30 MPa bound is a case-author screening figure in that regime, not a measured delamination limit; the declared 8e-6 m^2 tension section represents a support structure sharing the hoop load. The verified outcome: 200x2, the cheapest screening-passing candidate, is eliminated by the pressure bound alone (36.6 MPa > 30 MPa while its hoop stress and utilization pass), so the bound demonstrably changes the selected optimum. Prices are invented placeholders; the result is a modeled screening outcome under declared bounds, never a production or mechanical-acceptance claim. The pressure estimate itself is a first-order screen -- no pack stiffness, insulation compliance or stress redistribution is modeled, and its value depends on the declared sampling plan.",
